{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 40, :comments ["<b>Fruit of a tree hadar.</b> A tree whose taste of its wood and its fruit are the same (Sukkah 35)." "<b>Hadar.</b> That remains (הַדָּר) on its tree from year to year — and this is the etrog (ibid.)." "<b>Kappat temarim.</b> Missing a vav — this teaches that it is only one." "<b>And a branch of a tree avot.</b> Whose branches are woven like braids (עֲבוֹתוֹת) and like cords — and this is the hadas, which is made in the manner of braiding (ibid. 32)."], :book :leviticus, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 23, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T09:08:02.832842794Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}